From a5e1c698e16bb84beb759a25d1141e257a0b6cea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fsm_core <you@example.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 19:53:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add graph serialization: to_dict/from_dict,
 to_json/from_json, to_bson/from_bson
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- BaseNode: self-registering type registry (__pydantic_init_subclass__)
  so custom node subclasses round-trip to the right class.
- GraphEngine.get_all_nodes() / add_existing_node() — public accessors
  needed to (de)serialize nodes not reachable from root.
- GraphEngine.to_dict()/from_dict() — structural snapshot (nodes + edges
  + root), edges rebuilt through the existing add_node() so cycle checks
  aren't duplicated.
- to_json()/from_json() via stdlib json (no new dependency).
- to_bson()/from_bson() via lazily-imported bson; raises SerializationError
  with an install hint if the optional 'bson' extra isn't installed.
- New SerializationError(CoreError) exception.
- setup.py: extras_require['bson'] = ['pymongo>=4.0'].
- tests/test_serialization.py: round trip, custom subclass, orphan nodes,
  invalid JSON, dangling child ref, unknown type, missing-bson error,
  real bson round trip.
